@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title GitHub credentials — init stores them, a run only lifts, seed never logs in

' covers: cmd/proveo/ghtoken.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_github.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init.go
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
'   git identity (sibling) .... _spec/_paradigms/git-identity.puml
'   the store name that injects _spec/internal/sbx/credential-path.puml
'   SSH remotes in the clone .. _spec/packages/lib/github-ssh-hosts.puml

node "Host — proveo init (once, TTY)" as INITHOST <<host>> {
  component "verify gh · install via brew/apt/dnf/winget\nelse name https://cli.github.com/" as INST <<app>>
  component """gh auth login""" as LOGIN <<app>>
  component """gh auth token --hostname github.com""\nbounded 5s" as GH <<app>>
  database "macOS login KEYCHAIN\nthe default `gh auth login` store" as KC <<db>>
  database "~/.config/gh/hosts.yml\ntoken only when gh put one there" as HOSTS <<db>>
  database "sbx secret store\nservice github (builtin)" as STORE <<db>>
}

node "Host — proveo run (each launch)" as RUNHOST <<host>> {
  component "GITHUB_TOKEN / GH_TOKEN\nexplicit env" as ENV <<app>>
  component "lift token · never login" as LIFT <<app>>
}

node "Container — seed" as CONT <<host>> {
  component "-e GH_TOKEN  (BARE name)" as FWD <<app>>
  component "_proveo_github_token\nubi recipes 5000/hr" as UBI <<app>>
  component "gh / git (baked in every image)" as TOOLS <<app>>
}

component "token on the docker argv\nvisible in ""ps""" as LEAK <<error>>
component "anonymous 60/hr per SOURCE IP\nsilent loss of code intelligence" as ANON <<error>>
component "git push: could not read Username" as PUSH <<error>>

INST ARROW_OPTIONAL LOGIN : gh missing
LOGIN ARROW_MAIN KC : gh stores it; proveo keeps no copy
ENV ARROW_MAIN LIFT : first match wins
KC ARROW_MAIN GH : reachable ONLY from the host
HOSTS ARROW_OPTIONAL GH : often holds no token
GH ARROW_MAIN LIFT
GH ARROW_MAIN STORE : sbx secret set github\nvalue on stdin, --force
LIFT ARROW_MAIN FWD
STORE ARROW_OPTIONAL CONT : sbx proxy injects git HTTPS\nand api.github.com
FWD ARROW_MAIN UBI
FWD ARROW_ERROR LEAK : what the bare name AVOIDS
UBI ARROW_ERROR ANON : when no token is reachable
STORE ARROW_ERROR PUSH : when init never wrote github

note bottom of HOSTS
  **The false premise.** ""ghConfigMount"" binds ~/.config/gh read-only so ""gh""
  inside the container reuses the operator's session, and its rationale assumed
  hosts.yml holds the OAuth token. That is true only when gh stored one there —
  ""--with-token"", CI, or a host with no system keyring.

  The default macOS flow puts the token in the login keychain and leaves
  hosts.yml with a username and nothing else. The mount then lands a config with
  no credential: ""gh auth token"" inside the container returns empty, and the
  entrypoint's own check has always reported "gh session not authenticated".
end note

note right of GH
  Bounded at 5s, mirroring the cap the entrypoint puts on ""gh auth status"". A
  warm keychain answers in ~30ms, but a LOCKED one blocks behind a GUI
  authorization prompt a CLI run can never satisfy — and a timeout is reported
  as its own case, because telling an operator who IS logged in to run
  ""gh auth login"" sends them down the wrong path.

  ""--hostname github.com"" is pinned because ubi resolves against api.github.com:
  an operator authenticated only to a GitHub Enterprise host must fall through
  to unauthenticated rather than forward a token that host will reject.
end note

note right of LIFT
  A run only LIFTS. Login moved to ""proveo init"" because it needs a browser
  and a terminal a headless or already-inside-sandbox run does not have.
  Missing credentials warn and point at init; they never open ""gh auth login"".

  The lift still forwards by BARE name so the value comes from proveo's own
  environment rather than the docker argv. Seed's ""_proveo_github_token"" only
  READS that env (or in-container ""gh auth token"") for mise/ubi — it does
  not install gh, does not login, does not ""sbx secret set"".
end note

note bottom of STORE
  **Service name, not GH_TOKEN.** sbx's proxy injects for builtin ""github"".
  A store entry named for the env var is one the proxy never reads, so init
  writes ""sbx secret set --force github"" with the value on stdin. That is
  host-wide, not ""--sandbox NAME"": proveo readies the operator's machine,
  not a Cursor sandbox it is running inside.

  This assumes github.com is how the host pushes. A GitLab origin still
  benefits from the token (ubi rate limits) and skips the proxy path. Better
  than nothing; the operator can pick ""later"" on the init row.
end note

note bottom of LOGIN
  Init is the one TTY. ""--yes"" / no terminal still stores a token that is
  already in env or in gh's store, and will not invent a login or run brew.
  A declined or failed gh step is not a failed init — same as ""sbx setup"".
end note
@enduml
